title AMUS3 — Constel wire: the handshake framed for a local wire, whole and lawful
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress before checking in, send often as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think AMUS2 (handshake) landed the three proven values — Greeting, Ack, Session. The Constel README's road-on named the next rung: carry those values across a wire. Crux-first, Lindy-first, gate-free: a self-describing frame is read on its ten-thousandth day and carries the constellation's safety into every byte that will ever move — the durable move, and the hardest still-tractable one, above one-off features.
think The pattern is CAUM1 (mikrophone/wire.rye), proven: magic · version · length · Sha256 digest · payload, every check run before a byte is yielded. AMUS3 carries it to the three handshake values with a tagged layout — magic CNST · version · kind(1=Greeting 2=Ack 3=Session) · payload_len · digest · payload — one source of truth so a reader offset can never drift. Each payload is a bounded length-prefixed serialization of the value's own fields; per-kind ceilings so a tampered Ack cannot claim Greeting room.
think What makes it more than a copy of CAUM1: deframing is TWO independent gates. The Sha256 proves the payload WHOLE (no byte flipped); the naming law re-run at the border (check_ship / check_constellation / never_a_ship on every name) proves it LAWFUL (no vowel-bearing, real-@p-shaped name smuggled in). A payload passes only when both hold. The AMUS-specific proof: a vowel smuggled into a payload whose digest was FIXED UP still refuses VowelPresent — integrity alone can never carry a real address across a Constel channel.
obs First build failed: WireError declared || name.NameError but the deframe re-checks reach for handshake's own NotAMember and SameParty. Widened to || handshake.HandshakeError (which already unions name.NameError). Named error at the border, verify-before-trust — a red caught by the compiler and closed by the witness on metal, not a claim.
obs Witness proves on metal across four blocks: each of the three values round-trips byte-for-byte; a short, bad-magic, bad-version, bad-kind, overlong, truncated, tampered, and wrong-kind frame each refuses by name before a value is formed; a smuggled vowel with a fixed-up digest still refuses VowelPresent at the border; and a field length prefix past the payload refuses FieldOverrun. Witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, width exit 0. Prior rungs (handshake, roster) stay GREEN — strictly additive.
obs Kept docs synced in the same round (docs-implementation-sync): constel/README.md gains the wire.rye rung, the run block lists amus_wire_witness, Status and Kin weave include AMUS3, and the road-on now names AMUS4 (a two-party exchange loop over the frames), AMUS5 (an in-process byte queue), and AMUS6 (the real Comlink transport) — so the remaining Comlink-seam crossing is sized and named without being reached.
loom witness=amus_wire_witness blocks=4 kinds=3 max_frame_bytes=126 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
file active-designing/20260814-043551_amus3-constel-local-wire-frame.md the AMUS3 design — the tagged frame, the two-gate deframe, the four-round quest naming AMUS3–AMUS6
file constel/wire.rye AMUS3 — frame/deframe the three handshake values, verify-before-trust with the naming law at the border
file tools/amus_wire_witness.rish the GREEN witness for AMUS3
file constel/README.md kept synced — the wire rung, run block, Status, Kin, and the AMUS4–AMUS6 road-on
recommend keep-going — AMUS3 GREEN and ready to send; the next agent-doable AMUS rung (AMUS4) composes an exchange loop over these frames, still purely local and gate-free. AMUS6 (real Comlink transport) is the eventual check-in (Claude) point before touching seed/comlink/. No custody gate reached. Clock note: America/New_York read 20260814.044105, earlier than the prior newest 075400; the one-clock monotonic law honored by stamping 075900, just after the work it follows.
